<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="stateUpdated" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[SeqCtrl: Handles the basic logic for state transitions and HMI handling for sequences. 

To Use:
	- Place on a rung that runs every scan BEFORE any of the steps
	- Map/set the mode input to True (1) to disable HMI control. 
	- Map/Set the disableHmiStart input to True (1) to disable the HMI start button, typically for when the safety system is not in a safe state.

Sequences, written externally, should always be interacted with by using the following inputs:
- cmdStart
- cmdAbort
- cmdPause
- nextStep

NEVER write directly to currentStep.

See AIC Wiki for more details]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Change the startup step on first scan/power on
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(S:FS)MOVE(startupStep,currentStep)MOVE(startupStep,nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Use a bool and jump label to updated the state (running/aborted/etc) bits twice. 
- Once here at the beginning before we check what commands are valid, and 
- a second time at the end once the step has been updated]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(stateUpdated)JMP(updateState);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(begin)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set the current "mode"
need to have a pseudo-automode when running code so that IO will respond, but system is not in full running/automode]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(mode)XIO(autoModeOverride)OTE(hmiModeSel);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   HMI Button Handling   /////////

When valid, set the corresponding PLC command(s) when the HMI requests it. HMI should Set On the commands (once) and this program will turn them off.

Start Button]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(hmiCmdStart)ONS(internalOns.1)[XIO(hmiModeSel) XIO(disableHmiStart) OTL(cmdStart) OTL(autoModeOverride) ,OTU(hmiCmdStart) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Start Button Visibility]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(hmiModeSel)XIO(disableHmiStart)[XIC(complete) ,XIC(paused) ,XIC(aborted) ]OTE(hmiStartVisible);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Abort]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(hmiCmdAbort)ONS(internalOns.2)[XIO(hmiModeSel) OTL(cmdAbort) OTL(autoModeOverride) ,OTU(hmiCmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Abort Button Visibility]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(hmiModeSel)XIO(complete)XIO(aborted)OTE(hmiAbortVisible);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pause (Hold)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(hmiCmdPause)ONS(internalOns.4)[XIO(hmiModeSel) OTL(cmdPause) OTL(autoModeOverride) ,OTU(hmiCmdPause) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Hold Button Visibility]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(hmiModeSel)[XIC(running) ,XIC(pausing) ,XIC(restarting) ]OTE(hmiPauseVisible);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset AutoMode Override]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(aborted) ONS(internalOns.7) ,XIC(complete) ONS(internalOns.8) ,XIC(paused) ONS(internalOns.9) ]OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[In Active State: a shortcut to check if the sequence is running code vs is in and idle state]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(running) ,XIC(pausing) ,XIC(restarting) ,XIC(aborting) ]OTE(inAnActiveState);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Reject Invalid CMDs   /////////

Prevents random bits from getting latched on and causing unexpected execution


]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdAbort)[XIC(complete) ,XIC(aborting) ,XIC(aborted) ]OTU(cmdAbort)OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdStart)XIO(complete)XIO(aborted)XIO(paused)OTU(cmdStart)OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdPause)XIO(running)XIO(restarting)OTU(cmdPause)OTU(autoModeOverride);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Parse Commands and Transition States   //////////

Any state transition that requires a command should be handled here. Exceptions are:
- going from running to complete
- going from pausing to paused
- going from aborting to aborted

Respond to start command. Varies based on state]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdStart)[[XIC(complete) ,XIC(aborted) ] MOVE(0,nextStep) ,XIC(paused) MOVE(5000,nextStep) ,OTU(cmdStart) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Respond to pause command

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdPause)[MOVE(3000,nextStep) ,ONS(internalOns.13) [MOVE(currentStep,stepBeforePause) ,XIC(running) MOVE(currentStep,runningStepBeforePause) ] ,OTU(cmdPause) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Respond to Abort Command

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(cmdAbort)[MOVE(6000,nextStep) ,ONS(internalOns.12) MOVE(currentStep,stepBeforeAbort) ,OTU(cmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Step Control   /////////

Enable autoStep to run code normally
Disable autoStep and manually toggle singleStep for control of sequence execution

NOTE: This should be last rung of any sort of step control logic so that all parsing and checks of commands happen before the step number acutally changes.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(autoStep) ,XIC(singleStep) ][MOVE(nextStep,currentStep) ,OTU(singleStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(updateState)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Set Status Bits   /////////


Running Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(0,currentStep,1999)OTE(running);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Complete Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(currentStep,2000)OTE(complete);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pausing Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(3000,currentStep,3999)OTE(pausing);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Paused Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(currentStep,4000)OTE(paused);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Restarting Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(5000,currentStep,5999)OTE(restarting);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Aborting Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(6000,currentStep,6999)OTE(aborting);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Aborted Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(currentStep,7000)OTE(aborted);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Use stateUpdated bit to call this chunk of code twice. Once at the beginning in case someone messed with currentStep and then at the end in normal order to reflect what changed]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(stateUpdated)OTL(stateUpdated)JMP(begin);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(stateUpdated);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Faulted Status   /////////

Set faulted status bit if any fault bit is set on]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(fault,0)OTE(faulted);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Create a bit addressed state output for HMIs with limited functionality (like C-More or View Studio)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(running)OTE(state.0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(complete)OTE(state.1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(pausing)OTE(state.2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(paused)OTE(state.3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(restarting)OTE(state.4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(aborting)OTE(state.5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(aborted)OTE(state.6);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
<Tags/>
<Programs>
<Program Name="Camera" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="Main" Disabled="false" UseAsFolder="false">
<Tags>
<Tag Name="camera" TagType="Base" DataType="AicCamera" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[[0,0,0],[0]]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="AicCamera">
<StructureMember Name="in" DataType="AicCameraIn">
<DataValueMember Name="running" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="faulted" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="inspectionCount" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="result" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</StructureMember>
<StructureMember Name="out" DataType="AicCameraOut">
<DataValueMember Name="start" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="stop" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="trigger" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</StructureMember>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="cameraMinOffTime" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[-1610449746,500,500]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="500"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="500"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="cameraTimeout" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,2000,0]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="2000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="camSeq" TagType="Base" DataType="SeqCtrl" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Comments>
<Comment Operand=".FAULT.0">
<![CDATA[camera took too long]]>
</Comment>
<Comment Operand=".FAULT.1">
<![CDATA[camera did not start]]>
</Comment>
</Comments>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[33689607,7000,7000,0,0,5000,0,0,64,7000,128,[0,2000,0]]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="SeqCtrl">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="mode" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="autoModeOverride" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="disableHmiStart" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="faulted" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="running" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="complete" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="pausing" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="paused" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="restarting" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="aborting" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="aborted" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="inAnActiveState" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="cmdStart" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="cmdPause" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="cmdAbort" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="autoStep" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="singleStep" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiCmdStart" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiCmdPause" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiCmdAbort" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiStartVisible" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiPauseVisible" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="hmiAbortVisible" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="currentStep" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="7000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="nextStep" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="7000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="fault" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ons" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="stepBeforeAbort" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="5000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="stepBeforePause" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="runningStepBeforePause" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="state" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="64"/>
<DataValueMember Name="startupStep" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="7000"/>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="camStartTimeout" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,1000,0]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="1000"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="camTriggerPulseTime" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[365847,250,0]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="250"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="exampleTrigger" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="inspectionCycleTime" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Output" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="lastInspectionCnt" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="lastResult" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="waitForResults" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,100,0]]]>
</Data>
<Data Format="Decorated">
<Structure DataType="TIMER">
<DataValueMember Name="PRE" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="100"/>
<DataValueMember Name="ACC" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="TT" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="DN" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</Data>
</Tag>
</Tags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="CameraSequence" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[<Put your sequence description here. What does it do?>]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[//////////   Prescan   /////////

Enforce a minimum time between triggers. The camera usually only react so quickly

### Modify as needed ###]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(camera.out.trigger)TON(cameraMinOffTime,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Abort if the camera faults or stops while running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(camSeq.running)[XIC(camera.in.faulted) GT(camSeq.currentStep,0) ,XIO(camera.in.running) GT(camSeq.currentStep,0) ]OTL(camSeq.cmdAbort);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Sequence Status and Control   /////////

### set mode and disableHmiStart accordingly ###]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SeqCtrl(camSeq,1,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Running   /////////

Steps 0 - 1999.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,0)MOVE(0,camSeq.fault)OTU(camera.in.faulted)MOVE(100,camSeq.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Make sure the camera process is running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,100)[XIO(camera.in.running) ONS(camSeq.ons.0) OTL(camera.out.start) ,XIC(camera.in.running) OTU(camera.out.start) MOVE(500,camSeq.nextStep) ,TON(camStartTimeout,?,?) ,XIC(camStartTimeout.DN) OTL(camSeq.fault.1) OTL(camSeq.cmdAbort) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Wait for a trigger, turn on lights, etc.

### Modify as needed ###]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,500)XIC(exampleTrigger)MOVE(1000,camSeq.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/// Trigger the camera ///

Start the camera and log the last inspection count value (used to determine when the camera process is done)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,1000)XIC(cameraMinOffTime.DN)[OTL(camera.out.trigger) ,MOVE(camera.in.inspectionCount,lastInspectionCnt) ,MOVE(1100,camSeq.nextStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[automatically turn off the trigger and set a timer to ensure its off for a few scans so 
the PC has a chance to see the change. The Python script will only trigger on a rising edge.

### Modify as needed ###
Exact speed can vary with PC and process]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(camera.out.trigger) TON(camTriggerPulseTime,?,?) ,XIC(camTriggerPulseTime.DN) OTU(camera.out.trigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Wait for the inspection count to increment (meaning we have a new result), and the parse the result

Abort if the camera takes too long

Store the camera timeout as an approx measure of inspection end-to-end latency]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,1100)[NE(camera.in.inspectionCount,lastInspectionCnt) MOVE(1110,camSeq.nextStep) ,TON(cameraTimeout,?,?) ,XIC(cameraTimeout.DN) OTL(camSeq.fault.0) OTL(camSeq.cmdAbort) ,MOVE(cameraTimeout.ACC,inspectionCycleTime) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Wait for results. 

Very occassionally they don't seem to arrive at the same time as the inspection cnt since
tag writes can get split apart into multiple packets]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,1110)[TON(waitForResults,?,?) ,XIC(waitForResults.DN) MOVE(1120,camSeq.nextStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Parse the results

### Modify as needed ###]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,1120)[MOVE(camera.in.result,lastResult) ,MOVE(1900,camSeq.nextStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[### Modify as needed ###

Turn off lights, clean up results, reloop if desired, etc]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,1900)MOVE(2000,camSeq.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   COMPLETE   /////////

Step 2000. Done. Waiting for start command to go back to beginning of running. 
Step transition handled by SeqCtrl AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   ABORTING   /////////

Don't need to stop camera process on abort. It will sit idle waiting for a trigger.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(camSeq.currentStep,6000)MOVE(7000,camSeq.nextStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[/////////   Aborted   /////////

Step 7000. Program Stopped/Canceled. Waiting for start to go back to beginning of running.
Step transition handled by SeqCtrl AOI]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Main" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(CameraSequence,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
